**Goal:** trace one user action from a click to the server and back, and know which file owns each step.

Foldkit is the browser UI framework in rat-stack. A Foldkit program keeps its state in a Model. Events arrive as Messages.

An `update` function takes the Model and a Message, and returns a new Model plus any Commands. A Command is a named task that runs outside `update` and ends by sending another Message.

The docs browser at `/search` is the worked example. Its search box calls the [search capability](/lore/one-capability-every-surface).

## 1. The view sends a Message

The Search button sends `SubmittedSearch`. The view does no fetching.

```ts repo=rat-stack path=apps/web/src/features/app.ts at=a3f5a14861ce89913e82bea0f7ba02c83e8d4725 lines=224-229 {226} title="A click is a Message"

```

Every Message the program accepts is declared in one union:

```ts repo=rat-stack path=apps/web/src/client/docs/message.ts at=a3f5a14861ce89913e82bea0f7ba02c83e8d4725 lines=7-22 {17-18,20} title="SubmittedSearch, SucceededSearch, FailedSearch"

```

## 2. update returns a Command

`update` sets the search to `Loading`, increases a generation counter, and returns the `SearchDocs` Command:

```ts repo=rat-stack path=apps/web/src/features/app.ts at=a3f5a14861ce89913e82bea0f7ba02c83e8d4725 lines=35-42 {39-40} title="Loading now; the search runs as a Command"

```

`update` does no I/O. It describes the next Model and the work to run.

## 3. The Command calls the capability over RPC

```ts repo=rat-stack path=apps/web/src/client/docs/command.ts at=a3f5a14861ce89913e82bea0f7ba02c83e8d4725 lines=10-18 {13-15} title="SearchDocs ends in a result Message"

```

`DocumentQueries` builds its [RPC](/skills/learn-rat-stack) [client](/skills/uncomplect) from the shared contracts. The `rat-stack-boundaries/no-browser-server-imports` lint rule lets browser modules import `@rat-stack/core/contracts` and `@rat-stack/capability/rpc-group`, never a [handler](/systems/capabilities). [AGENTS.md](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/a3f5a14861ce89913e82bea0f7ba02c83e8d4725/AGENTS.md)

```ts repo=rat-stack path=apps/web/src/client/docs/queries.ts at=a3f5a14861ce89913e82bea0f7ba02c83e8d4725 lines=7-11 title="The client group comes from the contracts"

```

On the server, `implement` binds the same `searchContract` to the content store:

```ts repo=rat-stack path=apps/site/src/capabilities/search.ts at=a3f5a14861ce89913e82bea0f7ba02c83e8d4725 lines=7-11 title="The server stays authoritative"

```

## 4. update folds the result into the Model

```ts repo=rat-stack path=apps/web/src/features/app.ts at=a3f5a14861ce89913e82bea0f7ba02c83e8d4725 lines=141-146 {143} title="Only the latest search may land"

```

The generation check drops a stale reply. If the user searches twice, the first reply carries an old generation, and `update` keeps the Model unchanged.

## Why one path

Each step has one owner, so each step can be tested alone.

- The Model is data. The view reads it and sends Messages.
- `update` is a function of the Model and a Message. It runs without a network.
- In this program, only Commands call `DocumentQueries`, the RPC client. Each Command ends in a Message.
- The contract is the one [Schema](/lore/schemas-define-the-boundary) set that the browser and the server share.

`SearchState` names four states: `Idle`, `Loading`, `Loaded`, and `Failed`. The view matches on all four, so no flag combination can show a spinner and an error at once. [model.ts](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/a3f5a14861ce89913e82bea0f7ba02c83e8d4725/apps/web/src/client/docs/model.ts)

